{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הזה היום", :translit "ha-ze ha-yom", :gloss "this the day"} {:he "והיה כי יאמר אליך", :translit "ve-hayah ki yomar eilekha", :gloss "and it shall be when he says to you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut ha-parshiyot: the phrase הזה היום in v. 15 is read against the adjacent phrase והיה כי יאמר אליך in v. 16, so the word יום ('day') governs the piercing procedure."}], :frame {:text "The procedure of piercing the ear of the slave who refuses to go free (רציעה) is described in Deuteronomy 15:17. Ba'al HaTurim reads the word יום ('day') in v. 15 as a temporal qualifier on that procedure, restricting it to daylight hours.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 15:15" "Deuteronomy 15:16-17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut ha-parshiyot: the phrase הזה היום in v. 15 is read against the adjacent phrase והיה כי יאמר אליך in v. 16, so the word יום ('day') governs the piercing procedure.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:48.075583939Z", :model "glm-5.2"}